{"id":"DRKS00011208","src":"drks","title":"UMBRELLA Protocol SIOP-RTSG 2016 - Integrated research and guidelines for standardized diagnostics and therapy of kidney tumours in children, adolescents and young adults","official":"","summary":"This study will standardize the diagnostics of childhood kidney tumours including the use of biomaterial. This will allow the optimization of diagnosis including reference centres for all children with kidney tumours in participating centres from Germany, Europe and beyond Europe. The study is registering the diagnosis and treatment and will develop new biomarkers that will be used in the future for a better risk-adapted treatment resulting in better outcomes with less toxicity and late effects.","conditions":["Malignant neoplasm of kidney, except renal pelvis"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"Treatment of the different kidney tumours is not a subject of the study. This is done according to SIOP 2001 (DRKS-ID of the study:  DRKS00003769). The aim is to standardize diagnosis and and treatment in participating countries."}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\nAll children with a kidney Tumor and adults with nephroblastom if they are diagnosed in a participating centre. Participating centres have to register all such pateints into the UMBRELLA SIOP-RTSG 2016 protocol\nExclusion criteria:\nMissing informed consent is the only exclusion criterion.","minAge":"","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2019-03-01","pcd":"2027-12-31","upd":"2026-07-28","sponsor":"Saarland University","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Prof. Dr. Norbert Graf · Klinik für Pädiatrische Onkologie und HämatologieUniversitätsklinikum Homburg · 06841 1624711 · graf@uks.eu"],"sites":[{"f":"Reinhard-Nieter-Krankenhaus Städtische Kliniken gGmbH","city":"Wilhelmshaven","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":53.5476,"lon":8.1039},{"f":"Ostschweizer Kinderspital","city":"St. Gallen","zip":"","s":"R","